{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>I will cause all My goodness to pass before your face.</b> This will not be withheld on the grounds that I am One who does not grant grace, for indeed I will cause all My goodness to pass before your face." "<b>And I will proclaim in the name of YHWH before you.</b> One who proclaims in the name of YHWH is one who makes known and teaches the existence of the blessed El and the ways of His goodness. He said: if so, <b>I will cause all My goodness to pass before your face</b>, so that if the eyes of your understanding were sufficient for this, you would apprehend your entire desire; and therewith I will teach you to benefit from some of the ways of My goodness, through whose knowledge you will acquire some knowledge of My essence, as it says: וַיִּתְיַצֵּב עִמּוֹ שָׁם, וַיִּקְרָא בְשֵׁם ה' (Exodus 34:5)." "<b>And I will grace whom I grace.</b> I will grant you that grace which is My way to bestow upon everyone who finds favor in My eyes — namely, abundant bounty without any limitation and without narrowness of eye." "<b>And I will show compassion to whom I show compassion.</b> I will have compassion upon you so that you do not die from the radiance of the flash of My glory, as is My way to have compassion upon all who are worthy and fit for that, as it says: וְשַׂכֹּתִי כַפִּי עָלֶיךָ עַד עָבְרִי."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:59.966219220Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}